WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Troubleshooting is a skill, not a guess. We're going to build your diagnostic
process from the ground up.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Common AC failures and their diagnostic patterns. No cooling at all: check
power, contactor, capacitor, compressor. System runs but does not cool: check
charge (superheat/subcooling), airflow (filter, blower), and metering device.

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
Short Cycling: System turning on and off rapidly. Causes include oversized
equipment, low charge, and thermostat issues.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Pattern recognition speeds up diagnosis.
After enough service calls you will recognize common failure patterns
immediately.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: No cooling = power, contactor, capacitor, compressor. And —
Frozen coil = airflow or charge

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
You get a call — condenser fan not spinning, compressor humming. What's the
first thing you check? Answer that before you move on.

